# Pairs with ResizeCompletes. EnterRejectingAsync returns without moving the
# shard into Rejecting, so the flip, which waits for every shard to be fenced,
# never becomes enabled and a resize nobody undoes never completes. The fence
# step stays weakly fair; it simply achieves nothing.
MODULE: ResizeCompletesFenceNoOp
TARGET: ResizeCompletes
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: fencing a shard has no effect, so the alias flip never becomes enabled
PERTURBS: ResizeFence

--- FIND
    /\ s \in rzShards \ fence
    /\ fence' = fence \cup {s}
--- REPLACE
    /\ s \in rzShards \ fence
\* MUTATION: the fence is not recorded.
    /\ fence' = fence
--- END